  "body": "## What changed\n\nThis is wave 1 of #3190. It folds the 18 flat `crates/app/tests/turning_*.rs` binaries into the `turning` directory suite.\n\n- The 18 files move to `crates/app/tests/turning/<name>.rs` (git renames, 99-100 % similar).\n- `turning.rs` loads each file with `#[path = \"turning/<name>.rs\"] mod turning_<name>;`.\n- Each module keeps its old binary name. The test `turning_bore` / `x` is now `turning` / `turning_bore::x`.\n- Each submodule keeps its `//!` header, its Gate map and its lane line. `xtask` joins the Gate maps of all sources of a suite (`quick::gate_maps`).\n- `mod common;` becomes `use crate::common;`. Four files declared `common` and did not use it. Those lines are removed.\n- Two `include_str!` paths get one more `../`, because the files are one directory deeper.\n- `docs/decisions/3190-fold-turning-suite.md` records the choice of the wave and what was dropped.\n\nNo production code changes. No test body changes.\n\n## Cause\n\nEach `camcraft-app` test binary is about 100-130 MB. The turning domain had 19 binaries for 115 tests.\n\n## Tests\n\nThis is a test-layout refactor. No behaviour changes, so no test can fail before it. The proof is that the test set is the same:\n\n- Before (base `e4b08e95b`): `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test 'turning*' -- --list` gives 19 binaries, 115 tests, 0 ignored.\n- After: `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test turning -- --list` gives 1 binary, 115 tests, 0 ignored.\n- The sorted list of qualified names (`<old binary>::<test>`) before is equal to the sorted list of module paths after (`diff` is empty).\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test turning`: 115 passed, 0 failed, in about 6 s. It ran three times, all green.\n- Each temp file in these tests has its own prefix and the process id. No two submodules write the same path in the shared process.\n\nGate on the final head `6939377`:\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: plan `app:turning whole suite`, 1 step, ok (41 s).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --tests -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main --dry-run`: 1 step reached (`app heavy: turning`). The suite has 0 ignored tests, so the step runs no test. It was not run. This PR is `P6`, which gets no heavy step (AGENTS.md \"Heavy lanes at review\").\n- Trial merge with upstream/main `4d891498e`: clean. Upstream did not change any of the 19 files or `tests/common/` since the base.\n\nDisk (debug, Linux): the 18 old binaries took 2,306 MB. The folded binary takes 201 MB. That is about 2.1 GB less for each worktree.\n\nNote: on this host sccache did not answer for this worktree, so the gates ran with `CAMCRAFT_NO_SCCACHE=1`.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. No `.nc`, `.cl` or catalog file changes. No post or toolpath code changes, so the `example_catalog` suites were not run.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Windows and macOS builds of the folded suite.\n- The other domains of #3190. They are for later waves, so the issue stays open (`Refs #3190`).\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone. No open PR touches `turning.rs` or a `turning_*.rs` file.\n\nChangelog: none\n\nRefs #3190\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
